  rung 0  (F diag, Theta diag, Sigma diag)   logL = -47.9072602235

=== Entry gate: the factorisation contract ===

At r = 0 with diagonal Phi, Theta and Sigma the likelihood factorises,
so the joint fit must equal the sum of the univariate fits exactly.

  univariate 1 (p=2, q=0)   logL =     -27.1020487852
  univariate 2 (p=2, q=0)   logL =     -20.8052114381
                                 sum  =     -47.9072602233
                                 joint=     -47.9072602235
  (both sides untruncated; the fit's own logL, xi truncated at 1e-03, is -47.9072602235)

  crossing identity (joint - sum) = -1.578e-10   (tolerance 1.0e-06)   VERIFIED
  rung 1  (F diag, Theta diag, Sigma free)   logL = -44.3045648528
  rung 2  (F free, Theta free, Sigma free)   logL = -30.3138127270

